WEBVTT

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.890
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:31.230
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:39.000
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:45.100
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.880
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:57.590
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:04.560
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:12.490
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:20.170
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.400
The train to Tokyo will
arrive shortly.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.270
Please remain behind
the yellow line.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.610
Stop pushing!

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.150
Wait till we
get off.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.180
Watch it,
buddy!

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.310
Look out,
jerk!

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.650
The train will
soon depart.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.880
Please stand back
from the doors.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.150
Things are going just
as I planned!

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.860
Sounds good.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:15.060
Oh, yeah.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.030
What?

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.290
Oh, no! My wallet's
gone!

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.660
Mine's gone
too!

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:23.640
So's mine!

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.500
Mine, too!

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:29.100
The ring from my
boyfriend!

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.580
Ha! That was
a cinch.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.120
Yeah, and what
a haul!

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:40.760
Don't be stupid!

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.720
Ow!

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.460
That hurt!

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.550
Quit fiddling around with that!

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.750
We're pros,
remember.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.020
We've got to act cool.
Laid back and cool.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:55.130
FILE. 37
THE YAMANOTE
EXPRESS INCIDENT

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:02.040
Many young women have reported thefts
on the JR Keihin Tohoku Line recently.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.510
That's why I've asked
you here today.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:10.550
Headquarters requested our assistance
with this investigation.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:13.950
We're going to assist
in a larceny case?

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.780
Yes.

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:20.050
I know it's out of our jurisdiction, but we were
recommended by someone very high up.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.560
Oh, no!

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.550
Inspector Arizuka, again.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:28.840
Oh well... if he needs us, he needs us.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.960
We've been through it before.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.970
Aoi Futaba! Yoriko
Nikaidou!

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.310
Who, me?

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:38.040
Why does it have to be Aoi and me?

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:42.270
I suppose it's because
of your experience.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:48.050
Nikaidou, you won an award of merit
from the Superintendent-General.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.720
And Aoi, you are very experienced
with undercover investigations.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.820
At least, that's why I think
you were chosen.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.100
But, sir!

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.790
Those two can't handle this by themselves!

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:02.230
Well, I gave my word that there would
be only two people assisting.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.300
You did?

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:09.870
<i>"I guarantee you, I only need two</i>
<i>people to help solve this case!"</i>

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.610
<i>"Two, and only</i>
<i>two."</i>

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.840
<i>"That's ridiculous!</i>
<i>It's impossible!"</i>

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:18.320
<i>"No, it's not impossible for</i>
<i>my exceptional officers!"</i>

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:21.790
<i>"Are you sure? You don't have to go</i>
<i>overboard just to prove yourself."</i>

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:23.490
<i>"Uh..."</i>

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:26.290
<i>"Uh..."</i>
<i>"All right. Let's give this one to Bokuto."</i>

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.660
<i>"Here's what</i>
<i>we'll do..."</i>

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.790
<i>"When your two officers from Bokuto</i>
<i>Station solve this case..."</i>

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.800
<i>"...we'll forgive your staff for those</i>
<i>reports over the last six months..."</i>

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.530
<i>"...and it won't affect</i>
<i>the bonuses."</i>

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.110
<i>"Thank you very</i>
<i>much, sir!"</i>

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:43.800
<i>"If they screw this up, you</i>
<i>know what will happen."</i>

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.450
<i>"Resignation."</i>

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:48.310
<i>"Resignation."</i>
<i>"The two must report to Inspector Arizuka."</i>

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.890
Aoi, have you had to write any reports?

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.190
No.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.690
Me neither. Not even once.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.660
That shouldn't stop you from participating.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:07.070
The two of you are Bokuto
Station's pride and...

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:09.300
...no, you are our
shining stars!

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:13.340
That's right! And thieves
are a snap to deal with.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.710
Right, Miyuki?!

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.800
Uh, yeah, sure...

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:19.940
Good luck,
you two!

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:21.140
Uh...

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.810
Tsujimoto, Kobayakawa. I want
you to back them up.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.050
Yes, sir!

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:30.190
Ahh...

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.360
The train will
soon depart.

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:47.440
Please stand back
from the doors.

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:58.920
Can you hear
me all right?

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:01.350
Yes, no problem.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.220
Okay. Now
listen up.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:05.780
According to the
reports...

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:08.360
...the criminals are usually
at the front of the train.

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:12.730
And most of their attacks occur between
one and four in the afternoon.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:17.930
It's probably easier for them
to avoid rush hour.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:19.730
Well? How does
it look?

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:25.940
Nothing suspicious
looking, so far.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:29.180
Miyuki, I don't know if I can do this.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.010
Stop that whining!

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.710
Don't be so loud! You'll
blow our cover!

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:37.020
You've got to be serious
about this!

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:40.620
Everyone's bonus depends
on you guys!

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.160
I know that!

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:45.230
You're one to talk! You've
written the most reports!

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:49.540
We should stop talking because
people will start to notice.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.800
Contact us if anything
happens.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.170
Over and out.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:56.310
Roger.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.280
It's crowded,
huh?

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:15.450
Maybe those thieves
aren't at it today.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.130
I don't even care
anymore.

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:22.600
We've gone from Ohmiya to Ofune
and back three times now.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:25.130
I don't feel
very good.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:29.210
Me either. My legs are
swollen, too. Ooh!

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:31.610
Hmm? What's
the matter?

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:35.110
Ow!

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:38.620
Way to go, Aoi! You
caught him!

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:42.250
All right! Here comes
my bonus!

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.720
No, it's not what
you think.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:47.690
That hurts! What
are you doing?

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:48.830
Police!

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:51.090
I'm arresting you
for molestation!

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:54.390
Wait! You're
mistaken!

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:55.870
Save your
breath.

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:57.770
We're getting off at
the next station.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:07:59.200
I didn't mean any-
thing by it!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.430
Molestation is a very
serious offense.

00:08:01.610 --> 00:08:11.340
Ow!

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.780
Yow!

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:24.330
Another molester.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.160
That makes
five now.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:32.640
They're not removing all those reports on
us if we're only catching molesters!

00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:35.400
It's in Aoi's nature,
though.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:45.410
Thanks for looking
after this.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:46.880
Sure, no problem.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:55.220
We're supposed to be catching
thieves, Aoi, not molesters.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.400
I know that.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:00.270
But they abuse
women...

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:01.930
...and I can't just
ignore them.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:07.700
What if there's another theft while
we're dealing with the molesters?

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.640
Is something bothering
you, Yoriko?

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:13.300
No, not especially.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:16.470
Just, how come the guys
always go for you?

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:19.140
Huh?

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:30.630
<i>The thief!</i>

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:32.630
Yoriko!

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:33.870
There you are.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:35.630
There you are.
Thank you very much.

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.340
Uh-oh.

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:53.850
Ahh...

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.970
"Reserved for Senior Citizens"

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:20.750
What a thing to ask. Just when I was
enjoying that young lady's legs!

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:22.350
"A New Model for a New Generation!
NEW BNW Z3 Roadster"

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.150
Huh?

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:32.220
You can't go around flashing
your badge, Yoriko.

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:35.490
If the thieves see you, we'll never
be able to catch them.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:38.890
Yeah, I guess
you're right.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:57.290
You see what I see?

00:10:57.290 --> 00:11:00.080
Yeah, but they'd be trouble.

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:04.420
Don't be scared, those kinds of
people have tons of money.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.390
Let's do it!

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:12.030
The train will arrive
shortly.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.200
Okay, we'll go after that brief-
case. Keep your cool.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:17.430
Please remain behind the yellow line.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:19.510
Let's go.

00:11:31.550 --> 00:11:34.150
I'm exhausted.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:35.660
What the hell do you think you're doing?!

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.950
You want a fight, buddy?!

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.390
Yeah, you
bastard!

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.700
Aah! A fight!

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.670
It's that guy!

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:56.240
Yoriko!

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:56.840
Yeah!

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.380
Ah! Thief!

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:00.070
Hey, you!

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:01.850
Oh!

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:03.180
Oh no!

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:05.590
Stop right there!

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.150
Stop!

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:15.220
Police! Stop where
you are!

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:17.760
We didn't shake
them!

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:20.230
I said stop!

00:12:26.170 --> 00:12:28.330
All right, you stupid...
Hmm?

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:30.710
Wait a second...

00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:32.340
Freeze!

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:41.020
All right, don't try anything stupid.
Put the guns down.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:46.790
Who would have guessed there
would be guns in that case?

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.790
I told you they'd
be trouble.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:51.520
Don't waffle
on me now!

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.430
"Police"

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:56.330
Oh, no! My
police ID!

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:01.430
Don't move!
Get it.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:05.300
That'll be
useful.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:07.440
Use it to get to
the driver.

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:10.180
Sorry, Aoi.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.680
Now nothing's going
to stop us!

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.630
Miyuki!

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:29.900
Let's go, Natsumi!

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:31.340
Okay!

00:13:31.340 --> 00:13:33.000
Nitro, on!

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:48.350
Police! It's an emergency!
Open up!

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:51.150
But I'm trying to
run the train!

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:54.920
"For Ohmiya"

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:59.660
What's going
on, anyway?

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:01.890
Don't stop at the
next station.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:04.940
Just keep on going!
Got it?!

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.660
I can't do
that!

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:11.730
There's a control device called
the ATS on every car.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:17.150
So if there's a train in front, we'll
automatically come to a stop.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:19.650
Override it!

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:41.170
Hey, give me back
my police ID!

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.800
Clam up! We've gotta do
what we've gotta do.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.210
Hey, let me
handle it!

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:48.140
I want to negotiate with
headquarters.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:51.450
What? The train's
been hijacked!

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:53.820
The ATS?! That's
ridiculous!

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:55.510
It can't be
done!

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.420
Contact the police!
Hurry!

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:03.290
I'm sure you realize that if you
try pulling any stunts...

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:05.590
...this whole train will
become a blood bath.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.430
Listen to me!

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:11.390
I've got a gun to my head!
You've got to cooperate!

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:16.440
Sir! Police headquarters just called and
said to follow their instructions.

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:18.780
Shut down
the ATS!

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.900
Get the trains in front
off the main line!

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:30.050
Now the schedule's
all messed up!

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:33.920
Another urgent call from
the police, sir!

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:37.460
Okay, we've followed the
instructions. What now?

00:15:37.570 --> 00:15:40.430
What's that?! The
Yamanote Line?!

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.950
Nakajima! Are you ready?

00:15:56.950 --> 00:15:57.550
Yeah.

00:15:57.550 --> 00:15:59.520
We've got to get moving, Miyuki!

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.430
We're counting
on you, sir.

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:09.790
Sure.

00:16:09.900 --> 00:16:11.160
You're in good
hands...

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:15.220
I've always wanted to race
the Keihin Tohoku Line!

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:18.930
"Limited Express"

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:26.210
Damn them! I'll show them just how
great our Yamanote Line is!

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:35.180
The tracks are over two meters apart
at Ueno and Okachimachi stations...

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:36.880
...so there's no way for you
to jump on from there.

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:41.190
That leaves the stations at Uguisudani,
Nippori and Nishi Nippori.

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:44.160
According to
the police...

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:48.830
...the Keihin Tohoku train
is still at Nishi Nippori.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.110
Then it's got to be
Nippori Station.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.770
"Nippori"

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:57.540
At this rate, we'll be in Nippori
in five minutes.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:00.170
This is our only
chance.

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:02.340
It's okay, I know
you can do it!

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:03.510
Of course
I can.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:13.490
They're passing Ueno
Station now.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:16.960
We'll be passing
in 20 seconds.

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:18.660
What's that
guy doing?

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:19.990
Huh?

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:25.800
G-o...Good... L-u...

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:30.140
What'd he
say?

00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:32.280
It meant "Good
Luck."

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:45.520
What are you
trying to do?

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:48.560
We're going to end up at
the dead end in Ohmiya!

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:50.490
Sh... Shut up!

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:53.000
Then we'll just go back
the other way!

00:17:53.170 --> 00:17:54.660
Aoi! Yoriko!

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:56.130
Miyuki!

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:58.530
Look behind you
to the left!

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:01.360
Huh?

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:05.640
"Limited Express"

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:09.610
What? I've never heard of any express
train on the Yamanote Line.

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:13.950
Natsumi!

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.820
What's going on?!

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:16.820
Aoi!

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.410
Try to open
the door!

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:20.560
What are you going
to try to do?

00:18:30.070 --> 00:18:32.110
The driver controls the doors.

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:36.130
The driver controls the doors.
But the guy's got a gun!

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:39.910
I understand.

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:41.450
I'll give it
my best!

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:44.850
We're counting
on you, Aoi.

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:54.320
Aoi!

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:56.050
There's no time
to lose!

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.290
We'll be at the Nishi Nippori
Station in one minute!

00:18:58.470 --> 00:18:59.930
Uh!

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:04.440
Huh?!

00:19:24.190 --> 00:19:26.160
Ahh!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:36.730
<i>"What a play! Aoi Futaba</i>
<i>feints left..."</i>

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:39.860
<i>"...and makes a fan-</i>
<i>tastic shot!"</i>

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:47.240
Why, you!

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:49.540
You want a taste of this
or something?!

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:51.620
Your model guns were stolen?

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.020
Yeah.

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:56.120
I see. They're guns for
your location shoots.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:56.460
Yes.

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:57.690
And where did this happen?

00:19:57.690 --> 00:19:58.230
Kamata.

00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.660
I see.

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:01.120
Word just
came in.

00:20:01.230 --> 00:20:04.360
Those aren't real guns you've
got there. They're models.

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:06.360
What?!

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:13.640
Natsumi! Now's
your chance!

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:20.850
Huh?!

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:59.020
Well, the thieves on the Keihin
Tohoku Line were caught...

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:03.020
...and the case was completely
wrapped up.

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:09.150
And as promised, your reports will
be stricken from your bonuses.

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:17.660
These are all the reports required
from this last investigation.

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:22.430
Do you have anything to
say for yourselves?

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:24.170
No?

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:28.370
In that case, I have some
good news for you.

00:21:28.480 --> 00:21:35.580
If we do something about those molesters,
maybe these reports won't have to be filed.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:41.650
Seeing as we've got that
connection high up.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.430
Chief! What are
you thinking?!

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:46.200
I won't be a part of this!

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:47.830
I wouldn't mind, really.

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:50.330
No, anything but that!

00:21:54.310 --> 00:22:00.510
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:07.820
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:11.020 --> 00:22:17.320
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:17.430 --> 00:22:27.440
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:27.510 --> 00:22:41.410
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:41.760 --> 00:22:49.700
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:49.760 --> 00:22:58.270
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:58.510 --> 00:23:06.350
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:06.410 --> 00:23:15.880
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:23.360
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:26.760
"Ah! That guy..."

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:29.270
That guy will be joining
Bokuto Station!?

00:23:29.670 --> 00:23:32.900
According to my research he's gentle,
easy to get along with...

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:34.840
...eats a lot, and
is very strong.

00:23:34.940 --> 00:23:37.100
He's a momma's boy that
loves bananas.

00:23:37.210 --> 00:23:38.970
And he's single with
no wife or kids!

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.310
My, that's some research!

00:23:42.580 --> 00:23:45.210
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 38...

00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:45.420
..."That Man, Shouji Toukairin."

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:47.350
FILE. 3B
THAT MAN,
SHOUJI TOUKAIRIN

00:23:47.350 --> 00:23:49.920
Eats a lot and is very
strong, huh?
